     - Color dominance & inclusions: Color accounts for 50-70% of value; natural inclusions (*jardin*) are expected in authentic natural beryl.
     - Astrological alignment & wearing rules: Ruled by planet Mercury (Budh); worn primarily on the little finger (Kanishtika) of the dominant hand on Wednesday morning.
     - Setting & metal options: 14K/18K yellow gold, white gold, and Panchdhatu/silver settings.
     - Ring designs for men vs women: Men's heavier signet/band settings with protective bezel vs women's halo, solitaire, and cocktail designs.
     - Certification & lab authenticity: Insisting on GIA, IGI, or authorized gemological lab reports verifying natural origin and oil treatment disclosure.
   - **Common FAQs (answered across 2+ competitors)**:
     - Which finger should a panna stone ring be worn on? (Little finger of dominant hand).
     - What are the main benefits of wearing a panna stone ring? (Speech, memory, commerce, logical focus).
     - Can a panna stone ring be worn daily in gold? (Yes, but requires protective bezel/halo setting due to 7.5-8 Mohs hardness and natural inclusions).
     - How is panna stone ring price calculated? (Gemstone per-carat quality + gold purity net weight + making charges + 3% GST).
